      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Network IK broke Final IK scripts on basically anything inside of the armature. You used to be able to use Final IK to adjust many of the IK settings. They'd need to address that known issue with NetIK in order to allow changes to your avatar's IK again. It was handy for so much more than adjusting IK for model proportions.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-09-13T00:35:26.666Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Would be nice for people who make weird proportioned avatars to be able to adjust the IK so Elbows bend and arms fully extend or don't Hyper extend when they aren't even close. I have made many avatars with ranging proportions for the rigs and i know what kind of works to allow everything to bend and what doesnt. that said i wish i could have some of my weird rigs still work and bend normally and not have my arms constantly bent when they're straight Irl. Most anime and other models from ranging styles have almost unhumanoid proportions that just make it so difficult to attempt to not have arms bending whilst extending.",
